\subsection{Runtime Overhead}
\label{sec:runtime}

Table~\ref{tab:runtime} reports per-document inference time for each configuration.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\small
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{4pt}
\begin{tabular}{@{}lll rr@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Model} & \textbf{Dataset} & \textbf{Mode} & \textbf{Avg (s)} & \textbf{Overhead} \\
\midrule
\multirow{3}{*}{Qwen}
  & \multirow{3}{*}{SciERC}
    & Unconstrained & 8.69 & --- \\
  & & Grammar       & 8.82 & $+$1.4\% \\
  & & Full (S1)     & 6.76 & $-$22.2\% \\
\cmidrule(l){2-5}
\multirow{2}{*}{}
  & \multirow{2}{*}{DocRED}
    & Unconstrained & 19.76 & --- \\
  & & Full (S1)     & 20.40 & $+$3.2\% \\
\midrule
\multirow{2}{*}{Llama}
  & SciERC
    & Unconstrained & 2.81 & --- \\
  & & Full (S1)     & 4.33 & $+$53.8\% \\
\cmidrule(l){2-5}
  & \multirow{2}{*}{DocRED}
    & Unconstrained & 18.16 & --- \\
  & & Full (S1)     & 20.52 & $+$13.0\% \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\caption{Per-document inference time (wall-clock seconds, same GPU).
Grammar-only overhead is $\leq$4.2\% across all cells.
Post-hoc filtering is an $O(n)$ pass over predicted triples and adds negligible time.}
\label{tab:runtime}
\end{table}

Constrained decoding overhead ranges from $-$22\% to $+$54\% relative, with three of four (model, dataset) cells at $+$13\% or less.
The outlier---Llama-SciERC at $+$53.8\%---corresponds to only $+$1.5\,s absolute per document.
Qwen-SciERC exhibits a \emph{speedup} under full constraints ($-$22.2\%): schema-constrained decoding produces tighter outputs and avoids long noisy continuations that the unconstrained model occasionally emits before EOS.
Grammar-only overhead is consistently small ($\leq$4.2\%), indicating that the semantic layer's logit masking accounts for most of the incremental cost when present.

